<section class="mt-12 max-w-3xl space-y-5">
  <p>
    Health insurance is written so that understanding it is work. Not
    maliciously, necessarily — but the result is that most people don't know
    what their own plan covers, and find out at the worst possible moment,
    from a bill.
  </p>
  <p>
    Two jobs here: understanding the plan you have, and pushing back when
    they say no.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="mt-14">
  <h2 class="display text-2xl">Understanding it</h2>
  <div class="mt-6 grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
    <%= render Ui::CardComponent.new(title: "Your plan, in plain words") do %>
      <p class="text-sm text-soft">
        What you'd actually pay in the situations that come up, what's
        covered, and how to use the thing you're already paying for. Read
        from your own policy documents rather than from generalities.
      </p>
    <% end %>
    <%= render Ui::CardComponent.new(title: "Two plans, side by side") do %>
      <p class="text-sm text-soft">
        Open enrolment with a real comparison: what each costs your
        household given how your household actually uses healthcare, rather
        than which has the lower headline premium.
      </p>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="mt-14">
  <h2 class="display text-2xl">When they say no</h2>
  <div class="mt-6 grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
    <%= render Ui::CardComponent.new(title: "The appeal, drafted") do %>
      <p class="text-sm text-soft">
        From the denial letter itself. A formal appeal that cites what they
        actually said, in the register these letters are answered in — which
        is most of what makes one land.
      </p>
    <% end %>
    <%= render Ui::CardComponent.new(title: "The deadline, on your calendar") do %>
      <p class="text-sm text-soft">
        Appeals are time-boxed and the window is easy to lose. It lands as a
        real date beside everything else in your life, not as a line in a
        letter you filed.
      </p>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="mt-14 max-w-3xl">
  <h2 class="display text-2xl">Why this is worth real money</h2>
  <p class="mt-4 text-soft">
    A substantial share of denials are overturned when appealed, and a
    substantial share are never appealed at all. The gap between those two
    numbers isn't about who's right — it's about who had the time, the
    confidence, and a template. That's the gap this closes.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="mt-14 max-w-3xl">
  <h2 class="display text-2xl">What it won't claim</h2>
  <p class="mt-4 text-soft">
    It reads your documents and says what they say. It won't assert what
    your insurer must do under law where you live, or promise an appeal will
    succeed. Where a rule varies, it says so and tells you to check — a
    confident wrong citation is worse than none.
  </p>
</section>
